 "capsule": "The Republic of Venezuela in this 1811–1815 span denotes the First Republic, declared 5 July 1811 by the congress that broke from Spain under Francisco de Miranda, and the Second Republic proclaimed by Simón Bolívar in August 1813 after his Admirable Campaign. Both were short-lived: the First fell to royalist forces in 1812 after Miranda's capitulation, and the Second collapsed in 1814 under a royalist and llanero counter-offensive led by José Tomás Boves, driving Bolívar into exile. This revolutionary-era entity is distinct from the consolidated Venezuela that emerged after Gran Colombia's 1830 dissolution.",
